  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1236 PM CDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nDry this week with small chance (15-25%) of showers this weekend...\nHigher heights aloft, especially late this week, along with general\nhigh pressure leads to dry weather this week. Sharper trough does\ndeflect off the ridge this weekend, but main lift with this passes\nwell to the north. May see a few showers over the north Saturday\nnight, but it could easily end up staying dry given this pattern\nand trends. Lower heights early next week and a frontal boundary\noverhead may spur on a few showers, but again, not great chances.\n\nFog Potential...High pressure prevailing combined with nighttime \ncooling and light winds will result in the potential for at least \npatchy ground fog each night/morning through early Thursday morning.\nPatchy dense fog could occur.\n\nTemperatures...Above normal temperatures will be with us until\nfurther notice. Bar on this is getting lower though, as average \nhighs by this weekend (last full weekend of October) are in the \nlow to mid 50s. We'll easily be above that mark and NBM indicates \n30-50% chance of seeing over 70 for especially central WI Thursday\nthrough Sunday. Other than tonight and early next week, when lows\ncould drop into the 30s north, overnight lows will also be above \nnormal, mostly in the 40s. Other than a couple brief exceptions, \nlonger range guidance (ECMWF-AIFS and CFS) keeps the warmer and\ndrier trend going into November which matches the latest Week \n3-4 outlook from CPC.",
